  "hajjIfradData": "[{\"title\":\"Before the 8th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"subtitle\":\"Arrival and Makkah Activities\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Etiquette and Guidelines\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udcd6\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Intention and Covenant\",\"items\":[\"Anyone intending Hajj should consciously seek closeness to Allah Almighty, as the Prophet \uﷺ said: 'Deeds are judged by intentions.'\",\"Hajj is a golden opportunity for sincere repentance, renewing one's covenant with Allah, and abandoning all sins.\",\"Ensure all funding for your Hajj comes from pure, lawful wealth free from any doubt.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Spiritual Supplications\",\"items\":[\"O Allah, I ask You for Your love, and the love of those who love You, and the deeds that will bring me to Your love.\",\"O Allah, cleanse my sins with water, snow, and hail, and purify my heart from wrongdoing.\"],\"type\":\"dua\"}]},{\"name\":\"Ihram from the Miqat\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83e\udd32\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Instructions and Steps\",\"items\":[\"At or before the Miqat, bathe (Ghusl), and apply perfume to your body — not your garments (for men).\",\"Men wear two clean white seamless garments (Izar and Rida). Women wear regular modest covering without showing adornment, and must not wear a face-veil (Niqab) or gloves.\",\"Make the intention in your heart and pronounce the Talbiyah: \\\"Labbayk Allahumma Hajjan.\\\"\",\"Continue the Talbiyah: \\\"Labbayka Allahumma Labbayk, Labbayka la sharika laka Labbayk, innal-hamda wan-ni'mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika lak\\\" — until you throw the first pebble at Jamarat Al-Aqabah on Eid.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Ihram Prohibitions\",\"items\":[\"Cutting any hair or clipping nails.\",\"Applying perfume to the body or garments after making the intention.\",\"Covering the head with a fitted cap (for men), or wearing tailored clothes such as trousers or shirts (for men).\",\"Sexual intercourse and its preludes, and contracting marriage.\",\"Hunting land animals.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"},{\"title\":\"Common Ihram Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Crossing the Miqat without entering Ihram — whoever does this must offer a sacrifice (Fidyah).\",\"Believing that entering Ihram means only putting on the garments — the true Ihram is the intention.\",\"Baring the right shoulder (Idtiba) from the moment of dressing — the Sunnah is to keep it covered and bare it only during Tawaf Al-Qudum.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Tawaf Al-Qudum (Arrival)\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Tawaf Etiquette\",\"items\":[\"It is a Sunnah for the Mufrid and Qarin arriving in Makkah to perform Tawaf Al-Qudum as a greeting to the Sacred Mosque.\",\"Stop the Talbiyah when starting Tawaf. The man exposes his right shoulder (Idtiba) during this Tawaf only.\",\"The man performs Raml (brisk walking with short steps) during the first three circuits only.\",\"Start from the Black Stone keeping the Kaaba on your left, and complete 7 full circuits.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Supplications of Tawaf\",\"items\":[\"When touching or gesturing toward the Black Stone, say: 'Bismillah, Allahu Akbar.'\",\"Between the Yemeni corner and the Black Stone, say: \\\"Rabbana 'atina fid-dunya hasanah wa fil-akhirati hasanah wa qina 'adhaban-nar.\\\" (Our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.)\",\"There are no fixed supplications for each circuit of Tawaf — supplicate from the heart with whatever you wish.\"],\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"title\":\"Common Tawaf Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Pushing aggressively to kiss the Black Stone, causing harm to fellow pilgrims — a distant gesture suffices.\",\"Performing Raml (brisk walking) in all seven circuits — it is Sunnah only in the first three.\",\"Reciting supplications from booklets aloud in groups, disturbing other worshippers and reducing the spirit of devotion.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Station of Ibrahim\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4c\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The Two Rakahs of Tawaf\",\"items\":[\"After completing Tawaf, go to the Station of Ibrahim and recite: 'And take the standing place of Abraham as a place of prayer.'\",\"Pray two Rakahs behind the Station if possible, or anywhere in the Sacred Mosque.\",\"It is Sunnah to recite Surah Al-Kafirun in the first Rakah and Surah Al-Ikhlas in the second.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]},{\"name\":\"Zamzam Water\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udca7\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Drinking Zamzam\",\"items\":[\"After the two Rakahs, it is recommended to drink deeply from Zamzam water and pour some on your head.\",\"The Prophet \uﷺ said: 'Zamzam water is for whatever it is drunk for.'\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Supplication While Drinking\",\"items\":[\"O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, abundant provision, and healing from every illness.\"],\"type\":\"dua\"}]},{\"name\":\"Sa'i (Walking)\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udeb6\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Sa'i of Hajj\",\"items\":[\"The Mufrid and Qarin may perform the Sa'i of Hajj after Tawaf Al-Qudum, so they will not need to perform it again on Eid — only Tawaf Al-Ifadah will remain.\",\"Ascend to Mount Safa and recite the Quranic verse beginning with: 'Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the Signs of Allah...'\",\"Face the Qiblah, magnify Allah three times, and supplicate, then descend walking towards Marwah.\",\"Complete 7 laps: going from Safa to Marwah counts as one lap, and returning counts as another.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Supplications at Safa and Marwah\",\"items\":[\"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar. La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul mulku wa lahul hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. La ilaha illallahu wahdah, anjaza wa'dah, wa nasara 'abdah, wa hazamal-ahzaba wahdah.\"],\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"title\":\"Common Sa'i Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Women running between the two Green Markers — the brisk walk is only for men.\",\"Raising the hands at Safa and Marwah as if making the opening Takbeer of prayer — the Sunnah is to raise them like a normal supplication gesture.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Staying in Makkah\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfe8\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Waiting Peacefully\",\"items\":[\"The Mufrid remains in Makkah in his state of Ihram (no release).\",\"Use this time for voluntary Tawaf, prayer in the Sacred Mosque, and Quran recitation.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 8th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Tarwiyah - 8th Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Proceeding to Mina\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Acts of Tarwiyah\",\"items\":[\"The Mufrid pilgrim heads to Mina in his Ihram during the forenoon.\",\"He prays there: Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr of the 9th day.\",\"Shorten the 4-Rakah prayers to 2 Rakahs (Qasr) without combining them.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Important Note\",\"items\":[\"Going to Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah is a Sunnah, not obligatory. Whoever skips it and goes directly to Arafah has a valid Hajj with nothing owed.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 9th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Arafah - 9th Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Standing at Arafah\",\"emoji\":\"\u26f0\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The Greatest Pillar\",\"items\":[\"After sunrise, head from Mina to Arafah calmly while reciting the Talbiyah.\",\"Pray Dhuhr and Asr combined (Jam' Taqdeem) and shortened (Qasr) to dedicate time to supplication.\",\"Stand facing the Qiblah with raised hands, earnestly supplicating to Allah until sunset.\",\"Ascending the Mountain of Mercy (Jabal Al-Rahmah) is not required — all of Arafah is a standing place.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Best Supplication\",\"items\":[\"The best supplication is the supplication of the Day of Arafah. The best of what I and the Prophets before me said: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul mulku wa lahul hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir.'\"],\"type\":\"dua\"},{\"title\":\"Critical Mistakes at Arafah\",\"items\":[\"Standing outside the boundaries of Arafah (e.g., remaining in the valleys surrounding it) — whoever does not stand within Arafah's limits has no Hajj!\",\"Departing and leaving Arafah before sunset.\",\"Fasting on the Day of Arafah as a pilgrim — the Sunnah is to break the fast to preserve energy for supplication.\",\"Wasting this precious time in idle chatter, photography, and sleep.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Moving to Muzdalifah\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udf19\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Overnight and Prayers\",\"items\":[\"Immediately after sunset, depart calmly to Muzdalifah.\",\"Upon arrival, pray Maghrib (3 Rakahs) and Isha (2 Rakahs) combined (Jam' Ta'kheer).\",\"Stay overnight in Muzdalifah until Fajr, then stand at the Sacred Monument (Al-Mash'ar Al-Haram) supplicating until dawn is very clear.\",\"The Prophet \uﷺ made a concession for the elderly, weak, and women to depart Muzdalifah to Mina after midnight.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Common Muzdalifah Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Believing pebbles must be collected from Muzdalifah — they may be picked from anywhere in Makkah or Mina.\",\"Praying Maghrib and Isha on the road before reaching Muzdalifah — unless fearing that midnight will pass before arrival.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 10th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Sacrifice (Eid Al-Adha)\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Stoning Jamarat Al-Aqabah\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfaf\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"How to Stone\",\"items\":[\"On reaching Mina on Eid, head directly to the Major Pillar (Jamarat Al-Aqabah) and stone it with 7 consecutive pebbles.\",\"Say 'Allahu Akbar' with each throw.\",\"Cut off the Talbiyah immediately upon throwing the first pebble.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Common Stoning Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Throwing all 7 pebbles at once — this counts as only one throw, and the remaining six are void.\",\"Believing the pillar is an actual Satan and throwing shoes or cursing at it — this is ignorance contrary to the Sunnah.\",\"Using very large pebbles — the Sunnah is pebbles the size of a chickpea.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Slaughtering the Hady\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udc11\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Hady Rules for the Mufrid\",\"items\":[\"The Mufrid has no obligatory sacrifice — his Hajj is complete without it.\",\"If he wishes to offer a voluntary sacrifice to thank Allah, the reward is immense.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]},{\"name\":\"Shaving or Trimming\",\"emoji\":\"\u2702\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The First Partial Release\",\"items\":[\"Men shave the entire head (preferred) or trim evenly. Women cut a fingertip's length from the ends of their hair.\",\"After stoning and shaving, the First Partial Release (Tahallul Al-Awwal) is achieved — the pilgrim changes into regular clothes and everything is lawful except sexual relations.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Common Shaving Mistake\",\"items\":[\"Trimming only part of the head and leaving other parts — this is the forbidden Qaz'a (patchwork cut). The entire head must be covered evenly by shaving or trimming.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Tawaf Al-Ifadah and Sa'i\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The Second Pillar\",\"items\":[\"Descend to Makkah to perform Tawaf Al-Ifadah — a core pillar without which Hajj is invalid.\",\"Perform 7 circuits without Raml or exposing the shoulder (Idtiba).\",\"After it, the Complete Release (Tahallul Al-Akbar) is achieved — everything including sexual relations is lawful.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Note for the Mufrid\",\"items\":[\"If the Mufrid already performed Sa'i after Tawaf Al-Qudum on the first day, no further Sa'i is needed now — Tawaf Al-Ifadah alone suffices.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Days of Tashreeq\",\"subtitle\":\"11th, 12th, 13th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Stoning the Three Jamarat\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfaf\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Rules of Stoning\",\"items\":[\"The stoning window during Tashreeq begins after Zawal (when Dhuhr prayer time enters).\",\"Stone the Small Pillar (7 pebbles), then move forward and supplicate at length facing the Qiblah.\",\"Stone the Middle Pillar (7 pebbles), then move forward and supplicate at length.\",\"Stone the Major Pillar of Aqabah (7 pebbles), then depart without making supplication after it.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Tashreeq Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Stoning before Zawal (early in the morning) — the majority of scholars consider this invalid.\",\"Stoning out of the prescribed order (e.g., starting with the Major then the Middle) — the correct order is Smallest, Middle, then Major.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Staying in Mina\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Obligation of Staying\",\"items\":[\"Staying in Mina during the nights of Tashreeq is obligatory — fulfilled by spending the majority of each night within Mina's boundaries.\",\"It is permissible to leave early on the 12th of Thul-Hijjah, provided one exits Mina's boundaries before sunset.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Concluding the Rites\",\"subtitle\":\"Departure and Farewell Tawaf\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Farewell Tawaf\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Final Act in Makkah\",\"items\":[\"The Farewell Tawaf is obligatory for every pilgrim leaving Makkah to return home.\",\"Perform 7 circuits with no Sa'i and no Raml.\",\"Women who are menstruating or experiencing postpartum bleeding are exempted.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Farewell Mistakes\",\"items\":[\"Remaining in Makkah for hours of shopping or sleeping after performing the Farewell Tawaf — the Tawaf must be the very last act before actual departure.\",\"Walking out of the Sacred Mosque backwards — this is an unfounded innovation not established in the Sunnah.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]}]",
  "hajjQiranData": "[{\"title\":\"Before the 8th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"subtitle\":\"Arrival for the Qarin\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Intention of Qiran\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83e\udd32\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Combining Both Intentions\",\"items\":[\"The pilgrim bathes and puts on the Ihram garments at the Miqat.\",\"He makes the intention in his heart and pronounces the Talbiyah combining both rites: \\\"Labbayk Allahumma 'Umratan wa Hajjan\\\" (Here I am, O Allah, for Umrah and Hajj together).\",\"The Qarin does not exit Ihram at all after reaching Makkah — he remains fully in Ihram until the Day of Eid.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Guidance\",\"items\":[\"Know, dear Qarin, that your acts of Hajj are an exact mirror of the Mufrid's — the only difference is that the Qarin must offer the Hady (sacrifice) on Eid, and his intention covers both Hajj and Umrah.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Tawaf Al-Qudum and Sa'i\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Tawaf and Sa'i\",\"items\":[\"The Qarin performs 7 circuits (Tawaf Al-Qudum) — a Sunnah.\",\"He should perform Idtiba (exposing right shoulder) and Raml in this Tawaf.\",\"He may perform Sa'i after this Tawaf, which will serve as his Hajj Sa'i and remove the obligation of repeating it on Eid.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Common Mistake\",\"items\":[\"The Qarin shaving his hair and releasing from Ihram after Tawaf and Sa'i, thinking it was a regular Umrah — he must remain in Ihram until the Day of Eid.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 8th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Tarwiyah - 8th Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Proceeding to Mina\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Acts of Tarwiyah\",\"items\":[\"The Qarin, still wearing his Ihram garments, heads to Mina during the forenoon.\",\"He prays Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr of the 9th day shortened (Qasr) without combining.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 9th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Arafah - 9th Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Standing at Arafah and Muzdalifah\",\"emoji\":\"\u26f0\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The Greatest Day of Supplication\",\"items\":[\"The Qarin heads from Mina to Arafah after sunrise.\",\"He prays Dhuhr and Asr combined (Jam' Taqdeem) and shortened (Qasr).\",\"He stands humbly supplicating to Allah until sunset.\",\"After sunset, he departs to Muzdalifah, prays Maghrib and Isha combined (Jam' Ta'kheer), and spends the night there.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Transmitted Supplication\",\"items\":[\"La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul mulku wa lahul hamdu, biyadihil khayru wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir.\"],\"type\":\"dua\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 10th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Sacrifice (Eid)\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Acts of Eid Day\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfaf\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Recommended Order\",\"items\":[\"1. Stone Jamarat Al-Aqabah with 7 pebbles.\",\"2. Slaughter the Hady (a sheep) — obligatory for the Qarin who joined both rites.\",\"3. Shave or trim the hair (achieving the First Partial Release).\",\"4. Perform Tawaf Al-Ifadah.\",\"5. No Sa'i is required if he already performed it after Tawaf Al-Qudum.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Hady Warning\",\"items\":[\"Purchasing a sick or defective animal (e.g., one that is one-eyed or visibly lame) — it is strongly recommended to delegate official bodies to ensure a sound Hady that reaches those in need.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Days of Tashreeq and Farewell\",\"subtitle\":\"11th, 12th, 13th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Stoning and Overnight Stay\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Completing the Rites\",\"items\":[\"Spend the nights of Tashreeq in Mina.\",\"Stone all three pillars each day after Zawal (Smallest, Middle, Major).\",\"When ready to travel, perform Farewell Tawaf (7 circuits) and depart immediately.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Reminder\",\"items\":[\"Stoning before the Dhuhr Adhan on the days of Tashreeq is not permissible — if done, it must be repeated.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]}]",
  "hajjTamattuData": "[{\"title\":\"Before the 8th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"subtitle\":\"Performing Umrah and Releasing Ihram\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Intention for Tamattu (Umrah)\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udcd6\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Beginning with Umrah\",\"items\":[\"The Tamattu pilgrim performs a full Umrah first, then releases from Ihram, then re-enters Ihram for Hajj on the Day of Tarwiyah.\",\"At the Miqat, he bathes, puts on the Ihram garments, and intends Umrah only, saying: \\\"Labbayk Allahumma 'Umratan mutamatti'an biha ilal-Hajj.\\\" (Here I am O Allah for Umrah, benefiting from it until Hajj.)\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]},{\"name\":\"Tawaf and Sa'i\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"A Complete Umrah\",\"items\":[\"He arrives in Makkah and performs 7 circuits of Tawaf with the intention of Umrah, with Raml and Idtiba.\",\"He prays two Rakahs behind the Station and drinks from Zamzam.\",\"He ascends Safa and performs Sa'i between Safa and Marwah (7 laps) for Umrah.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]},{\"name\":\"Trimming and Release\",\"emoji\":\"\u2702\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Completing the Umrah\",\"items\":[\"The Tamattu pilgrim trims his hair (not shaves — saving the shave for Hajj).\",\"Upon trimming, the Umrah is complete and he fully exits Ihram, wears normal clothes, and all prohibitions are lifted until the 8th of Thul-Hijjah.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Common Trimming Mistake\",\"items\":[\"Trimming only one side of the head — the obligation is to trim evenly across the entire head for it to be valid.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 8th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Tarwiyah and Ihram for Hajj\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Entering Ihram for Hajj\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83e\udd32\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Intention of Hajj from Makkah\",\"items\":[\"On the forenoon of the 8th, the Mutamatti bathes, applies perfume, and puts on the Ihram garments.\",\"He enters Ihram for Hajj from his residence in Makkah (his hotel) — no travel to the Miqat or Al-Tan'eem is needed.\",\"He recites the Talbiyah: \\\"Labbayk Allahumma Hajjan.\\\"\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Warning\",\"items\":[\"A common mistake: the Tamattu pilgrim goes outside Makkah (to Al-Tan'eem) to enter Ihram for Hajj from there — the Sunnah is to enter Ihram from his place of residence.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]},{\"name\":\"Heading to Mina\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Acts of Tarwiyah\",\"items\":[\"He heads with the pilgrims to Mina to pray Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr of the 9th day shortened (Qasr) without combining.\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 9th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Arafah and Muzdalifah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Arafah and Muzdalifah\",\"emoji\":\"\u26f0\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"The Greatest Pillar\",\"items\":[\"He heads from Mina to Arafah after sunrise.\",\"He prays Dhuhr and Asr combined (Jam' Taqdeem) and shortened.\",\"He dedicates the entire time to heartfelt, tearful supplication until sunset.\",\"After sunset, he departs to Muzdalifah, prays Maghrib and Isha, and spends the night there.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Supplication\",\"items\":[\"Rabbana 'atina fid-dunya hasanatan wa fil-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhaban-nar. (Our Lord! Grant us good in this world, good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.)\"],\"type\":\"dua\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"The 10th Day\",\"subtitle\":\"Day of Sacrifice (Eid)\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Eid Day Acts for the Mutamatti\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfaf\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Required Acts\",\"items\":[\"1. Stone Jamarat Al-Aqabah with 7 pebbles.\",\"2. Slaughter the Hady (a sheep) — strongly obligatory for the Mutamatti.\",\"3. Shave the entire head (shaving is now Sunnah).\"],\"type\":\"text\"}]},{\"name\":\"Tawaf and Sa'i for Hajj\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83d\udd4b\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Completing the Pillars\",\"items\":[\"4. Descend to Makkah to perform Tawaf Al-Ifadah.\",\"5. Perform Sa'i between Safa and Marwah (7 laps) for Hajj.\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"CRITICAL Warning\",\"items\":[\"The Tamattu pilgrim MUST perform Sa'i twice! His first Sa'i was for Umrah, and now he must perform it again for Hajj. Omitting this Sa'i invalidates the Hajj.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Days of Tashreeq and Farewell\",\"subtitle\":\"11th, 12th, 13th of Thul-Hijjah\",\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"Stoning and Conclusion\",\"emoji\":\"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Concluding Acts\",\"items\":[\"Spend the nights of Tashreeq in Mina.\",\"Stone all three pillars after Zawal each day.\",\"When ready to travel home, perform the Farewell Tawaf (7 circuits).\"],\"type\":\"text\"},{\"title\":\"Farewell Note\",\"items\":[\"A woman who is menstruating or in postpartum bleeding is exempted from the Farewell Tawaf — she travels directly without a penalty.\"],\"type\":\"warning\"}]}]}]",
  "instructionsListData": "[{\"title\":\"Hajj Al-Ifrad\",\"subtitle\":\"Ihram for Hajj only\",\"description\":\"The pilgrim enters Ihram for Hajj alone from the Miqat, saying (Labbayk Hajjan). He remains in Ihram until the Day of Eid, and no sacrifice (Hady) is required.\"},{\"title\":\"Hajj Al-Qiran\",\"subtitle\":\"Combining Hajj and Umrah together\",\"description\":\"The pilgrim enters Ihram for both Umrah and Hajj with a single intention, saying (Labbayk 'Umratan wa Hajjan). He remains in Ihram until Eid and must offer the Hady.\"},{\"title\":\"Hajj Al-Tamattu\",\"subtitle\":\"A full Umrah followed by Hajj\",\"description\":\"The pilgrim enters Ihram for Umrah during the Hajj months, saying (Labbayk 'Umratan mutamatti'an biha lil-Hajj). He performs Tawaf, Sa'i, and trims fully releasing Ihram, then re-enters Ihram for Hajj on the 8th of Thul-Hijjah. Hady is required.\"}]"
}